/target
**/target
# Keep guest lockfiles (needed for reproducible `cargo risczero build --locked`)
# and the root workspace lock committed for a deployable project.

# Generated work directories. Globs, not an enumeration: a new .demo-<x> from a
# future script must not slip through (this is the exact fragility that leaked a
# secret in another repository). These hold recipients.json and *.args, which
# carry recipient secrets.
.work
/.demo*/
/.linux-variant/
app/build
/app/build-linux/
/app/darwin-arm64/
/aqtinstall.log

# deploy-and-claim.sh writes distributions and their fresh run manifest here;
# artifacts/e2e/ itself is tracked (claims.tsv), so ignore only the run outputs.
/artifacts/e2e/dist*/
/artifacts/e2e/deploy-run.tsv

# Belt and suspenders, matched at any depth: these two files carry the recipient
# secret (nsk) wherever a script writes them, so they must never be committed
# even if a new work directory is missed above.
recipients.json
*.args

# Production files: the shooting script and the working draft of the
# submission live outside this repository. Both are build inputs, both were
# in French with stage directions, and one of them carried a line about other
# submissions to this programme that has no business in a public repository.
SUBMISSION-DRAFT.md
VIDEO_SCRIPT.*
